# A reference to a defaulted field is not a constant: an instance may set lim
# to anything, so the prior c?: <lim accepts {lim: 10, c: 9} and <5 does not.
-- old.cue --
lim: *5 | int
c?:  <lim
-- new.cue --
lim: *5 | int
c?:  <5
-- out --
unknown
c is constrained by lim in the prior schema and not in the new one; the checker cannot compare constraints between fields (rule unknown-crossfield) @ new.cue:2:1
